  ],
  "summary": "SoftBank Corp. and its subsidiary IDC Frontier are building a large AI data center in Tomakomai, Hokkaido, as the core site of SoftBank's Brain DataCenter concept. The plan, selected for a Japanese government regional data center subsidy in 2023, starts with a data center of about 50 MW, with receiving capacity expected to grow past 300 MW on a site of about 700,000 square meters. Ground was broken in April 2025 and SoftBank targets opening in fiscal 2026. The company intends to run the facility on renewable electricity sourced within Hokkaido.",
